     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "Ten million API requests hit Stripe servers every hour through a thirty-two character text string. Developers assume companies build software to sell finished apps. Modern tech giants print billions by putting digital tollbooths on individual lines of background code. An API key is a unique string that authenticates and tracks calls between separate software systems. Twilio generated over one billion dollars in revenue by charging fractions of a cent per SMS API call for apps like Uber. Uber calls the messaging endpoint millions of times daily. Every text message notification triggers a tiny micro transaction behind the scenes. OpenAI bills developers per text token processed through their API endpoints rather than selling raw software downloads. A single prompt generates thousands of tokens instantly. Metered rate limiting lets API providers throttle free users while automatically billing paid users based on live consumption. Free tiers hit strict walls once traffic scales up. Upgrading requires inserting a credit card directly into the developer dashboard. The code keeps running. The meter keeps ticking. Infrastructure becomes an infinite revenue stream."
